;  154    ! says when: reading a file, not a terminal). Then it has no carriage
;  155    ! control of its own, since its record already has one, and its first
;  156    ! piece is only as long as the record has room for after the prompt. The
;  157    ! log's records are always pieces of WIDTH, so the log is the same however
